<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Real-Time Budgeting & Rolling Forecasts</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Dynamic financial planning that transforms static annual budgets into living models, aligning 
            organizational targets with the evolving commercial reality.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Bottom-Up Budget Consolidation</h2>
        <p>
            The budgeting module empowers department heads and cost center managers to contribute 
            directly to the financial plan. Experience structured data entry with multi-level 
            consolidation, allowing for "bottom-up" planning that is then reviewed and 
            aligned with "top-down" strategic objectives. This collaborative approach 
            ensures that organizational targets are underpinned by operational reality 
            and possess genuine stakeholder buy-in.
        </p>
        <p>
            Historical actuals provide the baseline for budget entries, ensuring that 
            planning is informed by empirical performance data from previous periods.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Continuous Variance Analysis</h2>
        <p>
            Move beyond static once-a-year planning. The system provides real-time "Budget vs Actual" 
            variance analysis across every cost center, project, and business unit. Drilldown 
            capabilities from a variance figure directly to the underlying GL 
            transactions provide immediate clarity on why deviation occurred—whether due 
            to volume, price, or timing.
        </p>
        <p>
            Rolling forecast updates (e.g., "3+9," "6+6," "9+3") allow management to re-adjust 
            expectations based on latest performance, providing a more accurate view of 
            anticipated year-end outcomes than a fixed annual budget.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Strategic Scenario Modeling</h2>
        <p>
            Prepare for uncertainty with "What-if" scenario modeling. Test the impact of changes 
            in exchange rates, raw material costs, or market expansion across your 
            entire financial plan. This strategic intelligence allows leadership to 
            evaluate different organizational trajectories with data-driven confidence, 
            identifying both risks and opportunities well before they materialize on the 
            balance sheet.
        </p>
        <p>
            Executive KPIs for revenue growth, EBITDA margin, and operational spend 
            surface automatically, keeping leadership focused on the primary 
            financial drivers of organizational success.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

